{"_type":"item","id":"019dc140291979a49a8081bf91abe2ff","type":"dcr","status":"proposed","title":"Migrate PCBEditor from in-tree to plugin","description":"PCBEditor currently lives in-tree at `src/Scripts/UI/Controls/PCBEditor/` with ~2.5 KLOC of scene, data, canvas, and value-type code, plus `src/Scripts/Services/MCP/Modules/MCPPCBTools.gd` registering its 29 MCP tools into MinervaMCPServer. This DCR moves all of that into a plugin at `src/plugins/pcb/` (or the future minerva-plugins monorepo when that migration happens — see DCR `019da41ff6e571cc8262f19bd3586d52`).\n\n**Why this migration matters:** CAD validates the platform for greenfield plugins. PCB validates for rehosted existing editors — a different workflow with different failure modes (data-format compatibility, MCP tool re-registration patterns, annotation data migration, existing .minpcb files in the wild).\n\n**Key decisions already settled:**\n- PCB's existing annotation data (PCBAnnotation + PCBRouteHint) migrates to platform-registered annotation kinds (per DCR-2 plan decision comment). Route-hints become `pcb_route_hint` kind — domain-specific plugin extension, not structural data. See DCR-2 plan decision item 6.\n- Human=magenta, AI=cyan author colors preserved — lossless visual migration.\n- `.minpcb` file format stays compatible; annotations move from inline to sidecar (`foo.minpcb.annotations.json`).\n\n**Implementation strategy depends on Tier-2 availability:**\n- If DCR `019dc10364bf7f268c5c7dd07743c37f` (in-process GDScript plugin tier) has shipped by the time this executes → PCB is a pure-GDScript Tier-2 plugin. No Go shim, no subprocess. PCB's logic is entirely scene-side; no native compute needed.\n- If Tier-2 hasn't shipped → PCB is a Tier-1 plugin with a thin (~200 line) Go MCP shim that routes tool calls to the scene via the broker. Works, but unnecessary overhead.\n\nPriority is 3 because CAD needs to validate the platform first; doing PCB migration before CAD would lose the greenfield-validation signal. Not blocked strictly, but sequenced after CAD is real.\n\n**Acceptance:**\n- PCBEditor's directory is empty (or just a thin compatibility shim).\n- `.minpcb` files created with the in-tree PCBEditor open cleanly in the plugin version.\n- All 29 MCP tools work identically from the agent's perspective.\n- Annotations and route-hints round-trip through pack/unpack, including the migration from inline to sidecar.\n- Regression: existing dev PCB files load, save, and project-export without issue.","created_at":"2026-04-24T20:48:20","updated_at":"2026-07-07T20:53:17","priority":3,"tags":["migration","pcb","plugin"]}
{"_type":"item","id":"019dc140543c7256aa3fc88e77b7c2e0","type":"work_item","status":"backlog","title":"Plan: PCBEditor → plugin migration","description":"Sequence assumes CAD has shipped and validated the platform. If Tier-2 (in-process GDScript plugin) is available by execution time, MCP-tool-port strategy changes from \"thin Go shim\" to \"pure GDScript in-process.\" Tasks below are framed tier-agnostic where possible; tier-specific variants are called out in the individual tasks.","created_at":"2026-04-24T20:48:31","updated_at":"2026-04-24T20:48:31","tags":["migration","pcb","plan","plugin"],"parent":"minerva:019dc140291979a49a8081bf91abe2ff"}
