{"_type":"event","item_id":"019df41ace3b7d8fb1a132c607df0d1b","seq":4,"event_type":"transition","actor":"agent","timestamp":"2026-05-04T18:35:36","note":"in_progress → done. PIVOT: substrate change cancelled. Discovery: AnnotationV2Schema already has `lifecycle: String` ∈ {\"open\",\"applied\",\"resolved\",\"stale\"} as a required envelope field, validated, round-trips to plugins. Adding a separate `resolved: bool` would create two sources of truth. Instead: consumer-side change shipped — _summarize_annotation now derives resolved from lifecycle==\"resolved\" and surfaces lifecycle verbatim for callers wanting applied/stale. Tools in #6 will use lifecycle==\"resolved\" / \"open\" semantics; user-facing API stays as set_annotation_resolved(bool) mapping to lifecycle. Hint: 019df443eb8777be962510697cdaddad. Acceptance test added (123/0)."}
{"_type":"event","item_id":"019df41afdf2757fb1139f51368701c3","seq":1,"event_type":"created","timestamp":"2026-05-04T17:48:22","note":"Item created"}
