{"_type":"event","item_id":"019dfa68ad337ff683a9dd6cdf22adce","seq":3,"event_type":"transition","actor":"agent","timestamp":"2026-05-06T22:19:08","note":"open → in_progress. Pre-flight complete. Plan: generic FileWatcherService autoload (pub/sub, polling 2s, refcounted watch list) with DocumentRegistry as one client. T7 DoD scoped to buffer use case; service architected for plugin reuse via T7.5 (019dff5d27e4)."}
{"_type":"event","item_id":"019dfa68ad337ff683a9dd6cdf22adce","seq":4,"event_type":"transition","actor":"agent","timestamp":"2026-05-06T23:24:43","note":"in_progress → done. T7 done. Implementation:\n\n* Generic FileWatcherService autoload (RefCounted singleton + WatcherRuntime ticker Node) — pub/sub watch list with refcounted owners, polling at 2s. Justified in cold-review: stock Godot has no inotify binding, so polling is the only available change-detection strategy.\n* DocumentBuffer gained loaded_mtime/loaded_size snapshot fields (taken at construct/save/reload).\n* DocumentRegistry subscribes each buffer to FileWatcherService, dispatches file_changed: clean→reload_from_disk (silent no-op when disk matches buffer text), dirty→notify_external_change + external_change_pending signal with per-buffer prompt-open coalescing.\n* DiskAccess.stat() new helper.\n* MCPDiskTools._disk_write routes through registry.poke_path() so MCP-driven writes get the same dispatch + sync prompt firing.\n* WatcherRuntime autoload owns the Reload/Keep ConfirmationDialog (non-blocking modal); dialog dismissed automatically when buffer disposed via new buffer_disposed signal.\n\nCold-Opus review surfaced 5 SHOULD-FIX issues; all addressed:\n* #1 mtime granularity self-save race → dropped matches_disk_snapshot suppression in dispatcher; clean/dirty branch correctly handles every case (test_external_write_with_same_size_still_handled covers).\n* #3 reload-ordering race → clear_prompt_open before reload_from_disk in dialog handler.\n* #7 dispose dialog cleanup → new buffer_disposed signal + WatcherRuntime._on_buffer_disposed (test_dispose_emits_buffer_disposed_signal covers).\n* #8 owner_id coexistence → test_registry_and_plugin_can_coexist_on_same_path proves distinct owner_ids refcount cleanly.\n\nDoD verification:\n* 31 tests in test_external_change_watcher.gd cover all four DoD scenarios + coalescing + dispose-unwatch + poke + same-byte-length collision + dispose signal.\n* HITL: opened ~/temp/sub.tdsl in Minerva, edited externally via VSCode, dialog appeared with Reload/Keep buttons; Reload replaced text correctly, Keep preserved buffer; all four scenarios green.\n\nTest totals (across 10 suites): 327/0.\n\nHint 019dff63a031 (godot-headless-tests/new-class-name-needs-import-pass) saved — newly-added class_name files self-fail in --script mode until godot --headless --import refreshes the global script class cache."}
