{"_type":"event","item_id":"019dff5d27e476afafd227218cb3891a","seq":5,"event_type":"transition","actor":"agent","timestamp":"2026-05-06T23:24:57","note":"in_progress → done. T7.5 done. Three platform-reserved channels added to PluginScenePanelBroker:\n\n* host.fs.watch {path} — inbound RPC; resolves through PathResolver, registers FileWatcherService watch with owner_id \"plugin_panel:<plugin_id>:<panel_name>\".\n* host.fs.unwatch {path} — inbound RPC; releases the watch.\n* host.fs.changed {path,mtime,size} — outbound push via panel_root.receive(), bypassing manifest ipc_channels allowlist (mirrors attach_buffer/text_changed/detach_buffer pattern).\n\nImplementation:\n* Early intercept in handle_scene_request before normal channel-validation chain (channel == CHANNEL_HOST_FS_WATCH/UNWATCH).\n* Reverse map _fs_path_subscribers: {path: {panel_name: bool}} for fast push routing.\n* _ensure_fs_signal_connected lazily wires file_changed handler on first watch call.\n* _cleanup_fs_subscriptions called from unregister_panel + unregister_plugin_panels — auto-unwatches all of a panels watches via FileWatcherService.unwatch_all + walks reverse map.\n* Empty/bad path returns explicit {success:false, error:...} response (PathResolver gates).\n\nDoD verification:\n* test_plugin_scene_panel_broker_host_fs.gd — 16 tests covering RPC success, empty-path error, unwatch, push routing, post-unwatch silence, panel-detach auto-unwatch, two-panel shared-path push, payload integrity.\n* HITL: test_paired_dsl Panel.gd extended to call host.fs.watch on attach_buffer; FsChangedLabel updates on every external write to the .tdsl. User confirmed end-to-end via VSCode external edit.\n\nKnown gap (cold review item #4, comment 329): PathResolver is normalization-only — no path-level sandbox. Plugins can today watch /etc/passwd. Out of T7.5 scope per DCR. File a follow-up under PluginPolicy when sandbox semantics are designed (likely tied to permissions.filesystem.{mode,paths})."}
