{"_type":"event","item_id":"019dff96aa077cdda1911a95796da370","seq":4,"event_type":"transition","actor":"agent","timestamp":"2026-05-06T23:25:08","note":"in_progress → done. T7.6 closes with a \"no target\" finding.\n\nPre-flight goal: identify the external-file dependency vector for the CAD plugin to adopt host.fs.* against.\n\nFindings (from inspection of ~/github/plugins/cad and ~/github/plugins/cad/worker):\n* worker/mcad/lexer.py KEYWORDS list (lines 98-123) has no include / import / require / load token. The .mcad DSL is closed-world.\n* No import_stl / load_mesh / texture-load / external-file-read in worker/mcad/*.py. The only file references are export \"...\" directives — write-only output.\n* All examples (t_beam.mcad, t_beam_modular.mcad, t_beam_drilled.mcad, t_beam_conditional.mcad, mouse_body.mcad) are self-contained — modules and parameters defined inline.\n\nConclusion: CAD has no external-file dependencies to watch beyond the .mcad buffer itself, which is already covered by T7 via DocumentRegistry. Forcing CAD to adopt host.fs.* would be theater, not validation.\n\nT7.5 substrate stands on its own — the test_paired_dsl HITL fixture provides genuine end-to-end validation of the broker channels. First real plugin adopter will surface organically when a plugin with actual external dependencies arrives (a notes-sync plugin watching a folder, a future .mcad with includes, etc.).\n\nNo code change in this task."}
