{"_type":"event","item_id":"019e27b12f7c7e1d8ea02efc91fd1122","seq":4,"event_type":"transition","actor":"agent","timestamp":"2026-05-15T18:08:30","note":"in_progress → blocked. Abandoning the combined full-stack HITL. Root cause: the MCP surface needed to drive rule creation / enable / process from an LLM agent is path-driven and session-blind — see DCR 019e2cc988ec for the full audit.\n\nConcrete blockers:\n- No `library_*` MCP tools (rules require explicit `rules_path`).\n- No `session_state()` exposing open vaults/dirs/sources by label.\n- No path-free `process()` — caller must thread rules_path, registry_path, file_path.\n- Broker exposes no panel-state publish channel.\n\nResumption criterion: B1, B2, B3 under DCR 019e2cc988ec must be `done`. Then an LLM agent can read session state, insert library rules referencing destination labels, call process() and read a summary — all without paths in chat. This HITL test re-runs as a real agent-driven exercise at that point.\n\nW5b–W5h direct fixes (lazy destination registry + source-pane add button) are uncommitted scansort/ui edits, being committed in the same pre-Phase-1 cleanup pass alongside this transition."}
