{"_type":"event","item_id":"019e8f309807700288b6debf5dd1c823","seq":4,"event_type":"transition","actor":"agent","timestamp":"2026-06-03T22:01:37","note":"in_progress → done. DONE — core capability + tested seam landed; Go-client wiring split to follow-up 019e8f811497 (rubric decision: separable reusable infra, codetools has no host-request client yet).\n\nCORE (Minerva development @ 8e39e5bc): host.terminal.exec registered in ALLOWED_HOST_CAPABILITIES (PluginDefinition.gd:164); CapabilityBroker._handle_host_terminal_exec — prefers visible UI terminal (routed_through=terminal, exit_code best-effort since PTY can't read $?), else OS.execute subprocess (routed_through=headless, REAL exit code). Grant = trust boundary (no re-applied bash policy). Test test_host_capability_terminal.gd: 18/18 vs the REAL broker (await-frames + SingletonObject.plugin_capability_broker integration pattern — see hint 019e8f7bb815). Verified: app boots clean (compiles); hermetic suite 2/2 (no regression).\n\nSEAM (plugins main @ b62ce9c): bash_handler.set_host_exec_hook(fn) — approved command prefers host terminal when hook installed, None→local fallback; dormant until the Go client wires it; denied commands never reach the hook. 4 tests (worker 146 total); smoke tools=15.\n\nDoD status: capability gated/granted ✓ routes through terminal-or-headless ✓ clean fallback ✓ core fine without codetools ✓ regression green ✓. Deferred (follow-up 019e8f811497): the actual plugin→core round-trip (Go bidirectional host-request client). Hardening notes: headless timeout is advisory (OS.execute blocking); terminal-path exit code best-effort. Next: P2.3 hard removal."}
